// P03.26 (R11): the check of an instance for an abstract type argument does
// not look at every method of every instance: n methods x n abstract
// instances took 2.5 s and 2.7 GB at n = 4000 (quadratic). The held type
// arguments come from the declaration (heldParams, over its fields and method
// signatures), so it is linear. Accepted when the methods hold T behind a
// pointer, n errors when one method holds it by value. The .long test has the
// size 4000.
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-abstract-instances.py 400 ptr > %t.p.gopp
// RUN: timeout 10 %gopp check %t.p.gopp
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/gen-abstract-instances.py 400 value > %t.v.gopp
// RUN: not timeout 10 %gopp check --check-error-limit=0 %t.v.gopp 2>&1 | grep -c 'error\[E0389\]' | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: 800
